    crm:P129i_is_subject_of <https://mbdiaries.itatti.harvard.edu/diary/1903-04/document/47> ;
    crm:P183i_has_representation <https://ids.lib.harvard.edu/ids/iiif/493312317/full/full/0/default.jpg> ;
    rdf:value """the present. She was caressing and affectionate and charming, even more than usual. She has dismissed all her servants but two - evidently she is extremely  difficile , without her husband to restrain her.
In the evening Matthew Pritchard came to dine - an inarticulate but apparently honourable and intelligent Englishman. He used to be with Ned Warren, but they had some sort of a quarrel. Now he is secretary to the Director of the Museum
- upon whom, by the way, we called in the morning. Davis, it seems, is lending most of his pictures to the Museum for the winter. The famous forgery is to figure as “ The Donna Laura Minghetti Leonardo ” Good for Davis!
Pritchard was a great relief - we felt we could say anything we liked without “offending” him. """^^xsd:string ;
    mbdiaries-ontology:index 47 ;
    mbdiaries-ontology:part_of <https://mbdiaries.itatti.harvard.edu/resource/diary/1903-04> .

